WEBVTT

s1.1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.284
Symphony runs in two ways.

s1.2
00:00:02.284 --> 00:00:06.713
Kubernetes: k3s on one VM, or kind for evaluation.

s1.3
00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:08.755
There, each ticket gets its own pod.

s1.4
00:00:08.755 --> 00:00:12.343
Local mode: one process on the host, with no isolation.

s1.5
00:00:12.343 --> 00:00:14.137
Both use the same setup.

s2.1
00:00:14.487 --> 00:00:17.572
A new install starts with only Redis and the API.

s2.2
00:00:17.572 --> 00:00:21.616
You apply the manifests. They make empty Secrets that setup fills later.

s2.3
00:00:21.616 --> 00:00:24.892
You fill one Secret yourself, with a bootstrap admin token.

s2.4
00:00:24.892 --> 00:00:27.858
Then you log in with that token, and run symphony setup.

s2.5
00:00:27.858 --> 00:00:32.045
In local mode, the process prints an admin token at its first start.

s3.1
00:00:32.395 --> 00:00:35.312
Until setup is complete, the other components wait.

s3.2
00:00:35.312 --> 00:00:40.078
The daemon keeps its heartbeat, and logs daemon setup incomplete once a minute at most.

s3.3
00:00:40.078 --> 00:00:43.855
The merger idles, and logs merger not configured with what it lacks.

s3.4
00:00:43.855 --> 00:00:46.045
The assistant writes an idle heartbeat.

s3.5
00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:49.550
Health checks stay green, so Kubernetes does not restart them.

s3.6
00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.261
Jobs end with a setup incomplete event.

s4.1
00:00:52.611 --> 00:00:55.229
In a terminal, symphony setup starts the wizard.

s4.2
00:00:55.229 --> 00:00:58.290
It shows a progress bar, and does the GitHub App first.

s4.3
00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.392
A step that is done asks: Change it?

s4.4
00:01:00.392 --> 00:01:02.143
Secrets go into hidden prompts.

s4.5
00:01:02.143 --> 00:01:06.218
If the API refuses a value, you see why, and you can try again.

s4.6
00:01:06.218 --> 00:01:10.351
Scripts use one subcommand per step. Secrets come from standard input.

s4.7
00:01:10.351 --> 00:01:13.745
symphony setup --status prints the checklist.

s5.1
00:01:14.095 --> 00:01:16.332
Tern has the same flow in its Setup view.

s5.2
00:01:16.332 --> 00:01:20.326
Other people see a banner. For an admin, Setup opens by itself.

s5.3
00:01:20.326 --> 00:01:23.957
It shows the steps, the progress, and a card for the selected step.

s5.4
00:01:23.957 --> 00:01:25.498
Secret fields are masked.

s5.5
00:01:25.498 --> 00:01:28.697
A refused value is not saved, and the card says why.

s5.6
00:01:28.697 --> 00:01:31.384
A saved step shows what the API found.

s6.1
00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:37.307
Setup has eight steps. The API checks each value against the real service before it saves it.

s6.2
00:01:37.307 --> 00:01:38.801
Four steps are required.

s6.3
00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:42.964
Tracker: the Linear key and team, or the GitHub board and its status field.

s6.4
00:01:42.964 --> 00:01:47.938
GitHub App: it mints a token, lists the repositories, and reports missing permissions.

s6.5
00:01:47.938 --> 00:01:51.478
Repositories: the App must reach the default repository.

s6.6
00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:57.247
On Kubernetes, a running merger must also serve each repository. One merger serves them all.

s6.7
00:01:57.247 --> 00:02:00.744
Models: each role needs a stored key or a host credential.

s6.8
00:02:00.744 --> 00:02:02.193
Four steps are optional.

s6.9
00:02:02.193 --> 00:02:04.809
Notifications send a test message first.

s6.10
00:02:04.809 --> 00:02:09.206
The assistant checks the Slack tokens, and the Discord message content intent.

s6.11
00:02:09.206 --> 00:02:12.041
Webhooks wait for one signed delivery from each source.

s6.12
00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:16.352
Skills: the API fetches each skill source, and reports one that fails.

s6.13
00:02:16.352 --> 00:02:19.759
Setup is complete when every required step is done.

s7.1
00:02:20.109 --> 00:02:25.016
Credentials are write-only. No response, log or audit entry contains them.

s7.2
00:02:25.016 --> 00:02:27.648
On Kubernetes, they go into named Secrets.

s7.3
00:02:27.648 --> 00:02:31.358
In local mode, they go to secrets.env in the root directory.

s7.4
00:02:31.358 --> 00:02:32.769
Redis holds none of them.

s7.5
00:02:32.769 --> 00:02:36.133
Webhook secrets are the exception. Setup shows them once.

s7.6
00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.323
To get new ones, you rotate them.

s8.1
00:02:38.673 --> 00:02:43.050
On Kubernetes, a saved credential reaches the components through a restart.

s8.2
00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:47.198
The order is the daemon, the merger, the assistant, and the API last.

s8.3
00:02:47.198 --> 00:02:49.731
In local mode, a change applies at once.

s8.4
00:02:49.731 --> 00:02:54.379
SYMPHONY_PUBLIC_URL is the address where people and vendors reach the API.

s8.5
00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:59.690
Setup uses it for the webhook URLs. Without it, they use the address of the request.

s9.1
00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.969
When every required step is done, Symphony is ready.

s9.2
00:03:02.969 --> 00:03:05.926
Create your first ticket, and move it to an active state.

s9.3
00:03:05.926 --> 00:03:08.298
Follow it with symphony status, or in Tern.

s9.4
00:03:08.298 --> 00:03:12.183
The full guide is docs/install.md.
